{"resource":{"id":"go-common-mistakes","title":"Go — Common Mistakes","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"13 min","pages":18,"lastUpdated":"July 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"120+ common mistakes Go developers make — with wrong vs. correct code, debugging tips, and a prevention checklist."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Loop Variable Capture"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Nil Pointer Issues"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Slice Aliasing"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Race Conditions"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Goroutine Leaks"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Channel Deadlocks"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Error Handling"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Interface Mistakes"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Package Mistakes"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Performance"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Debugging Guide"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Prevention Checklist"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Best Practices","tag":"Programming","time":"17 min"},{"title":"Go — Tips & Tricks","tag":"Programming","time":"10 min"},{"title":"Go — Advanced Concepts","tag":"Programming","time":"25 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Recognise the 120+ most common Go mistakes at review time.</li>\n          <li>Fix them with idiomatic, race-free alternatives.</li>\n          <li>Build a debugging routine that catches regressions early.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Read with a linter open</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">golangci-lint catches many of these automatically. Turn it on before turning pages.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Loop Variable Capture</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Bad>for _, v := range items {\n    go func() { fmt.Println(v) }() // pre-1.22: all print last value\n}</Bad>\n        <Good>for _, v := range items {\n    v := v\n    go func() { fmt.Println(v) }()\n}</Good>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Nil Pointer Issues</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Nil map writes panic; nil map reads return zero. Nil slice appends work. Nil interface comparisons are subtle — a typed nil pointer inside an interface is not <code>== nil</code>.</p>\n        <Bad>var m map[string]int\nm[&quot;a&quot;] = 1 // panic</Bad>\n        <Good>m := map[string]int{}\nm[&quot;a&quot;] = 1</Good>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Slice Aliasing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>append</code> may return a slice that shares backing array with the input; mutating one mutates both.</p>\n        <Bad>b := append(a[:2], 99) // may overwrite a[2]</Bad>\n        <Good>b := append([]int{}, a[:2]...)\nb = append(b, 99)</Good>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Race Conditions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Concurrent map access without a mutex is undefined. Use <code>sync.Mutex</code> or <code>sync.Map</code>. Run <code>go test -race</code> in CI.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Race conditions: two goroutines write the same address without synchronization. -race flag surfaces them at runtime.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Goroutine Leaks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Goroutines blocked on unbuffered channels or missing <code>context</code> cancellation never exit. Always wire a deadline or done channel.</p>\n        <Bad>go func() { &lt;-ch }() // leaks if nothing ever sends</Bad>\n        <Good>go func() {\n    select {\n    case &lt;-ch:\n    case &lt;-ctx.Done():\n    }\n}()</Good>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Channel Deadlocks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Sending on an unbuffered channel with no receiver deadlocks. Closing a channel twice panics. Sending on a closed channel panics.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Error Handling Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Swallowing errors with <code>_</code>.</li>\n          <li>Comparing errors with <code>==</code> instead of <code>errors.Is</code>.</li>\n          <li>Losing context — always wrap with <code>%w</code>.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Interface Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Big interfaces are bad interfaces. Accept the smallest interface that satisfies the need. Don't declare interfaces at the producer — declare them at the consumer.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Package Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Circular imports — restructure into a domain package.</li>\n          <li>init() abuse — prefer explicit constructors.</li>\n          <li>Global state — pass dependencies.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Healthy package graph: DAG with no cycles, dependencies point toward domain.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Performance Problems</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Unnecessary allocations in hot loops.</li>\n          <li>String concatenation with <code>+=</code> instead of <code>strings.Builder</code>.</li>\n          <li>Unbounded goroutine spawning.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Debugging Guide</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Reproduce with the smallest input.</li>\n          <li>Add structured logs at boundaries.</li>\n          <li>Enable <code>-race</code> and <code>pprof</code>.</li>\n          <li>Use <code>dlv</code> for step-through when logs aren't enough.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Prevention Checklist</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>✅ golangci-lint in CI.</li>\n          <li>✅ <code>-race</code> in CI.</li>\n          <li>✅ Context on every I/O call.</li>\n          <li>✅ No naked goroutines — worker pool or errgroup.</li>\n          <li>✅ Wrapped errors with request-id.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Most Go bugs cluster around concurrency, slices, and error handling. A linter, the race detector, and code review catch 90% of them before production.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is the loop capture bug fixed?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — Go 1.22 changed loop-var scoping. Still worth knowing for older codebases.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is sync.Map faster?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Only for read-heavy workloads with disjoint keys per goroutine. Otherwise plain map + Mutex wins.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Race condition</strong> — unsynchronized concurrent access to shared state.</li>\n          <li><strong>Deadlock</strong> — every goroutine waiting on another.</li>\n          <li><strong>Goroutine leak</strong> — goroutine that never terminates.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Test in your context. Trademarks belong to their respective owners.</p>\n      </div></section>"}